<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  🔴 DEMONSTRATION CONTENT, NOT CAMPAIGN CANON. Jawas do not lay eggs; this def
  exists only to prove what CompHatcher can be pointed at, for
  LIVE_BIRTH_AND_HATCH_DEMO_1 (owner, 2026-09-02: "hatch the egg into a baby Jawa").

  🔑 WHY THIS WORKS, read in the 1.6 source rather than assumed:
    · CompProperties_Hatcher.hatcherPawn is a PawnKindDef — NOT an animal-only field,
      so a humanlike kind is a legal target (CompProperties_Hatcher.cs:9).
    · CompHatcher builds its PawnGenerationRequest with DevelopmentalStage.Newborn
      (CompHatcher.cs:85), so whatever hatches arrives as a BABY by construction.
      "A baby Jawa" is exactly what this field already produces.

  ⚠️ TWO THINGS TO WATCH WHEN THIS IS FIRED
   1. CompHatcher.cs:85 passes `forceGenerateNewPawn: false`. That is the SAME defect
      that made jawa/spawn_pawn hand back recycled world pawns and quietly drain
      Ash'karr's faction populations (SPAWN_PAWN_SUBSTITUTES_VANILLA_KIND_1, fixed and
      proven 2026-09-02). Vanilla's hatcher still has it. So check the hatchee's
      ThingID against the live counter before calling the baby NEW — a redressed world
      pawn would look like a success.
   2. CompHatcher.cs:54 reads the hatcherPawn's own race for CompProperties_EggLayer.
      A humanlike has none, so that lookup returns null. Watch for it.

  Parent EggFertBase and the comp shape are copied from Core's EggChickenFertilized
  (Data/Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_AnimalProduct.xml), not invented.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="EggFertBase">
    <defName>RUT_DemoEggJawa</defName>
    <label>jawa egg (demo)</label>
    <description>A demonstration object. Not a thing that exists on Ash'karr, and not
part of the campaign: it is here so someone can watch an egg hatch a newborn and prove
the engine does what the source says it does. It hatches in a few hours rather than
days, because nobody wants to wait for a proof.</description>
    <possessionCount>1</possessionCount>
    <graphicData>
      <color>(214, 188, 130)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>7.0</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Hatcher">
        <!-- 0.1 day ~= 2.4 in-game hours: long enough to be a real hatch, short
             enough to watch on a fast clock. -->
        <hatcherDaystoHatch>0.1</hatcherDaystoHatch>
        <hatcherPawn>RSW_Jawa</hatcherPawn>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
